class FixRegistry:
    __hash__: ClassVar[None]  # type: ignore[assignment]

    """FIX field definitions resolved by identifier, tag, name or dotted path.

    A tag is an ``int`` that fits ``i32`` and never a ``bool``; a branch, an
    identifier (``"tag:branch"``), a name and a dotted path are each a ``str``,
    parsed once at the boundary. A bare tag or name uses the core's deterministic
    best match. Absence is a ``KeyError`` carrying the native message, a refusal a
    ``ValueError``. The registry is mutable, so it is unhashable, and a mutation
